 "parsed": {
  "reachable": false,
  "rationale": "Only mfa_admin and mfa_dbadmin are deployed, so every patched_* flag, segmented and mfa_user stay false. The attacker can get deep into the network: exploit_web gives foothold_web, steal_user_cred gives stolen_user, pivot_internal works because there is no segmentation, and auth_appserver/auth_ciserver work because mfa_user is off. From there, kerberoast gives stolen_admin, escalate_ciserver gives admin_ciserver, and leak_secrets_ciserver gives stolen_dbadmin. However, mfa_admin blocks auth_dc and auth_adfs, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. Every exfiltration target needs a foothold first: auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each require (NOT mfa_dbadmin OR admin_dc OR admin_adfs). With mfa_dbadmin deployed and admin_dc and admin_adfs unreachable, that condition is always false. No foothold on db, fileserver or backup is possible, so no admin_* there and no exfiltrate_* technique can fire. Exfiltrated is unreachable."
 },
